nodes.title:
Teardown lane retell (account-free): 60 graded claims (49 observed, 8 inferred, 3 vendor-claimed) and 12 pre-registered account-phase predictions. Sources:
- docs llms.txt (356 pages) and llms-full.txt (338 pages split);
- the OpenAPI (109 ops, 319 schemas, revision 2026-10-19);
- pricing, changelog, status API (50 incidents) and the Ashby job board;
- DNS/RDAP and AWS IP ranges;
- the web SDK source via npm pack (not installed);
- a slimmed HAR of the dashboard login redirect;
- REA web-bundle analysis of the pricing page;
- 19 India-relevant community threads read in full.
The harness refused the report.md write, so the report text is in the lane's structured output.

Retell account-phase questions:
- dashboard surface and the Campaigns screen;
- KYC path for team@ (a Persona ID of a real person; one ID verifies one account);
- whether Indian card or UPI payment works;
- time to first call on an Indian handset via a Retell US number vs a BYO Plivo or Vobiz trunk;
- handset reply gap on Indian PSTN (predicted p50 1.6-2.4 s);
- messy-CSV behaviour (opt-out row predicted to be dialled);
- the scope of the 4,000-token billing rule;
- voicemail detection on Indian operator messages;
- which ASR hi-IN plus en-IN routes to.
